WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:17.588
let out a yell, and Zing let out a blast of flame before they both realized who had

2
00:00:17.648 --> 00:00:18.969
just burst into the cave.

3
00:00:18.989 --> 00:00:21.429
"Perda!" Zann exclaimed.

4
00:00:22.149 --> 00:00:24.330
"You shouldn't sneak up on people like that!"

5
00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:30.052
She smirked, quickly rubbing her fingers together and touching her arm to repair the spot where Zing had

6
00:00:30.112 --> 00:00:30.932
just singed her.

7
00:00:32.052 --> 00:00:35.894
"If you didn't want me in here, you should have used a Shield spell," she said.

8
00:00:35.914 --> 00:00:37.494
"What's the point?"

9
00:00:37.874 --> 00:00:38.415
Zann said.

10
00:00:38.435 --> 00:00:40.716
"You know all my passwords.

11
00:00:40.996 --> 00:00:42.916
You'd get past a Shield spell too."

12
00:00:42.936 --> 00:00:47.758
"True." Perda's smile faded quickly, and her eyes filled with worry.

13
00:00:47.778 --> 00:00:50.519
"But listen, I'm glad I found you.

14
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.881
Did you know your house—" "Just blew up?"

15
00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:55.301
Zann finished grimly.

16
00:00:56.042 --> 00:00:58.423
"Yes. Zing and I barely got away."

17
00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:00.123
"What about Boz?"

18
00:01:00.463 --> 00:01:01.704
Perda asked anxiously.

19
00:01:02.636 --> 00:01:04.778
"I don't think he was there," Zann said.

20
00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:09.382
"Here's what happened He told her the same story he'd just told Darb.

21
00:01:10.043 --> 00:01:11.184
Perda listened quietly.

22
00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:14.146
"Wow," she said when Zann had finished.

23
00:01:14.166 --> 00:01:16.368
"And you didn't recognize the guy?"

24
00:01:16.388 --> 00:01:20.531
"I've never seen him before in my life," Zann replied.

25
00:01:20.551 --> 00:01:22.533
"Did you check the Directory?"

26
00:01:23.214 --> 00:01:23.854
Zann blinked.

27
00:01:24.155 --> 00:01:25.175
Why hadn't he thought of that?

28
00:01:25.195 --> 00:01:30.320
"Um, not yet," he said, shooting a sheepish glance toward Darb.

29
00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.201
"We, uh, were just about to do that."

30
00:01:34.362 --> 00:01:35.603
"Here, I'll pull it up."

31
00:01:35.923 --> 00:01:37.044
Perda snapped her fingers.

32
00:01:37.744 --> 00:01:40.826
A book-like image appeared in midair, floating at eye level.

33
00:01:40.846 --> 00:01:43.767
"Identification needed," Zann said.

34
00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:45.068
"Adult male."

35
00:01:45.748 --> 00:01:49.771
Instantly the book disappeared, replaced by a long list of names.

36
00:01:50.631 --> 00:01:55.694
The names were in tiny print, since they represented every adult male in Magica.

37
00:01:56.755 --> 00:02:02.322
A picture floated beside each name, though the images were far too minuscule to be seen clearly.

38
00:02:03.002 --> 00:02:07.244
For a second Zann was tempted to check the list and see if his father was listed, or

39
00:02:07.325 --> 00:02:09.406
Boz. But he resisted the temptation.

40
00:02:10.066 --> 00:02:11.887
He had checked his father's listing before.

41
00:02:12.587 --> 00:02:19.371
It was still there, but with a special notation at the top: "Missing, presumed deceased or permanently off-world."

42
00:02:20.171 --> 00:02:25.014
As for Boz, it was too soon for his Directory status to have changed, no matter what had

43
00:02:25.054 --> 00:02:26.835
happened. "Well?"

44
00:02:27.115 --> 00:02:28.636
Perda said, sounding impatient.

45
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.661
"Is there anything else you can remember about this guy?

46
00:02:32.001 --> 00:02:33.921
You need to narrow the search down a little."

47
00:02:34.862 --> 00:02:36.242
"I know, I'm just thinking."

48
00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:39.123
Zann tried to remember what the stranger had looked like.

49
00:02:39.143 --> 00:02:41.743
"Uh, taller than average.

50
00:02:42.223 --> 00:02:43.164
Thinner than average.

51
00:02:43.944 --> 00:02:46.305
Between thirty and fifty years old."

52
00:02:47.065 --> 00:02:52.166
He watched as the list rearranged itself, the names getting bigger as their numbers became fewer.

53
00:02:52.186 --> 00:02:54.027
"Pale skin.

54
00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.947
Long, thinning dark hair."

55
00:02:55.967 --> 00:02:57.868
"What color were his eyes?"

56
00:02:58.248 --> 00:02:58.908
Perda prompted.

57
00:02:59.656 --> 00:03:00.677
"I'm trying to remember.

58
00:03:01.157 --> 00:03:05.038
I wasn't exactly gazing into his eyes at the time, you know," Zann said.

59
00:03:05.058 --> 00:03:06.539
"Here, I'll help."

60
00:03:07.279 --> 00:03:08.740
Perda held out both her hands.

61
00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.861
"Help with what?"

62
00:03:11.261 --> 00:03:14.643
Zann understood that she was offering to combine her magic with his.

63
00:03:15.423 --> 00:03:17.464
Anyone could do that to make a spell stronger.

64
00:03:18.104 --> 00:03:21.806
What he didn't understand was what spell she thought they should do.

65
00:03:22.586 --> 00:03:23.226
Perda sighed.

66
00:03:23.246 --> 00:03:26.908
"Don't you ever pay attention in Mental Magic class?

67
00:03:27.532 --> 00:03:30.793
We just covered Enhanced Short-term Memory spells last month!"

68
00:03:30.813 --> 00:03:32.633
"Oh, right."

69
00:03:32.974 --> 00:03:35.934
Zann lifted his own hands and rubbed his palms against hers.

70
00:03:36.735 --> 00:03:38.455
Sparks began to crackle between them.

71
00:03:38.475 --> 00:03:43.577
"Recall," he murmured, trying to focus on the memory of the man's face.

72
00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.497
Just like that the image popped into his head.

73
00:03:46.917 --> 00:03:49.958
It was as clear as if the stranger were standing right in front of him.

74
00:03:50.718 --> 00:03:53.559
Zann shuddered, quickly dropping his hands from Perda's.

75
00:03:53.579 --> 00:03:55.840
"Amber eyes," he said.

76
00:03:58.368 --> 00:04:01.411
"Small, mean-looking amber eyes, to be precise.

77
00:04:02.231 --> 00:04:04.173
Narrow face with sunken cheeks."

78
00:04:05.194 --> 00:04:07.896
He went on, adding as many details as he could.

79
00:04:08.677 --> 00:04:11.139
With each one the list of names grew shorter.

80
00:04:11.879 --> 00:04:14.762
Soon there were only a few names left on the floating screen.

81
00:04:15.502 --> 00:04:19.205
By now both names and images were large enough to see easily.

82
00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.607
"Do you recognize any of the pictures?"

83
00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.749
Darb asked, peering at the Directory.

84
00:04:23.769 --> 00:04:27.412
"I'm not sure Zann scanned the entries.

85
00:04:28.464 --> 00:04:30.926
"Wait! There he is—that's him!"

86
00:04:31.686 --> 00:04:33.227
Zann pointed at one of the images.

87
00:04:33.568 --> 00:04:35.829
Instantly all the other entries dropped away.

88
00:04:35.849 --> 00:04:37.811
"Full entry, please."

89
00:04:38.531 --> 00:04:40.653
More words appeared beneath the name and picture.

90
00:04:40.673 --> 00:04:44.135
"'Name: Morb,'" Perda read.

91
00:04:44.155 --> 00:04:47.357
"'Home: Dragon's Peak, Mount Mystery.

92
00:04:47.677 --> 00:04:49.659
Current Occupation: Unknown.'"

93
00:04:50.679 --> 00:04:51.800
"Dragon's Peak?"

94
00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:52.661
Zann said.

95
00:04:52.681 --> 00:04:56.163
"Isn't that the village that's always having trouble with trolls?"

96
00:04:56.183 --> 00:05:00.225
"Wait, this can't be the right person after all," Darb spoke up.

97
00:05:00.245 --> 00:05:02.245
"Look—he's a Void."

98
00:05:02.705 --> 00:05:04.366
He pointed to another part of the entry.

99
00:05:04.386 --> 00:05:05.966
"A Void?"

100
00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:06.947
Zann echoed.

101
00:05:07.247 --> 00:05:08.647
"But that doesn't make sense.

102
00:05:09.407 --> 00:05:12.048
This is definitely the guy that was at my house.

103
00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:15.729
Yet there's no way a Void could do what he did!

104
00:05:16.469 --> 00:05:17.610
The entry must be wrong."

105
00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.531
Perda moved her hand, causing the Directory to scroll down.

106
00:05:21.551 --> 00:05:23.891
"It can't be wrong," she said.

107
00:05:23.911 --> 00:05:26.372
"There are lots of mentions of him being a Void.

108
00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.562
See? It even says he used to work as an animal caretaker.

109
00:05:30.882 --> 00:05:31.962
That's a Void job."

110
00:05:32.883 --> 00:05:34.143
Zann glanced at the entry.

111
00:05:34.163 --> 00:05:36.624
"Wait, go back," he said.

112
00:05:36.644 --> 00:05:37.565
"Check it out.

113
00:05:38.305 --> 00:05:42.927
This Morb guy used to work at my parents' research laboratory at the university!"

114
00:05:42.947 --> 00:05:48.869
"Really? Then maybe Morb isn't connected to the royal warning at all," Perda suggested.

115
00:05:48.889 --> 00:05:51.851
"He might have been looking for your parents or something."

116
00:05:51.871 --> 00:05:54.512
"But he said he knew where Boz was.

117
00:05:55.284 --> 00:05:57.886
And why would he try to use the Flash Freeze on me?

118
00:05:58.627 --> 00:05:59.808
That doesn't make any sense."

119
00:05:59.828 --> 00:06:01.589
"Zann's right.

120
00:06:01.889 --> 00:06:05.853
This has to be connected to the disappearances of Reds somehow," Darb said.

121
00:06:05.873 --> 00:06:07.454
"I guess you're right."

122
00:06:07.754 --> 00:06:08.535
Perda gasped.

123
00:06:09.876 --> 00:06:11.677
"Gliss!" "Huh?"

124
00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:12.498
Zann said.

125
00:06:12.518 --> 00:06:16.701
"She's a Red, and so are both her parents," Perda said.

126
00:06:16.721 --> 00:06:20.945
"If Morb is after Reds, he'll probably try to get them too.

127
00:06:21.645 --> 00:06:22.986
We have to warn her!"
